Q: How to Insert an SF Symbol in a textField or a Label, as text, inn Swift A: <p>The problem is that the symbol is not a Unicode character, like a letter &quot;e&quot; or an emoji &quot;🙂&quot;. It is an <em>image</em>. The way to include an image in a run of text is as an attributed string with an NSTextAttachment.</p>
<p>Example:</p>
<pre class="lang-swift prettyprint-override"><code>class ViewController: UIViewController {
    @IBOutlet var label: UILabel!
    override func viewDidLoad() {
        super.viewDidLoad()
        let image = UIImage(systemName: &quot;pencil.and.outline&quot;)!
        let attributedText1 = NSMutableAttributedString(string: &quot;bouton &quot;)
        let attributedText2 = NSAttributedString(attachment: NSTextAttachment(image: image))
        attributedText1.append(attributedText2)
        label.attributedText = attributedText1
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>Result:</p>
